       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there is a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and shock. Overdoses can also cause non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and the effects can last a long time because the drug's half-life is long.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for frail or elderly patients or those with hepatic impairment\n\nIf 50 mg is what you intend, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it as a note. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy or your attending first. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
